@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-testing-bodies`

-- g5-tests-testing-bodies.l4: tests of g5-testing-bodies.l4 (ss.35 and 36).
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.35 and 36 (inputs/law.wiki lines 289 to 304) BEFORE any of
-- this was run.  A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so the rules are exercised with #TRACE, each with its
-- expected result written above it as `-- EXPECT:` and checked by work/g5/tracecheck.py.

§ `Tests of ss 35 and 36`

§§ `Fixtures`

--                            criminal  disciplinary  indictment  complaint
`no offences on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a conviction on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a pending indictment on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Standing: record, a conviction is for a disqualifying offence, the suspected offence would disqualify, an investigation is under way
--                                                           record                          conviction disqualifies  suspected disqualifies  investigation
`a clean standing`                         MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `no offences on record`,        FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a disqualifying conviction`               MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `a conviction on record`,       TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a conviction that does not disqualify`    MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `a conviction on record`,       FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a pending indictment for a disqualifying offence` MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `a pending indictment on record`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a pending indictment for a minor offence` MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `a pending indictment on record`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an investigation for a disqualifying offence` MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `no offences on record`,    FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`judgements with nothing on record`        MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `no offences on record`,        TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE

-- Person connected with the corporation: standing, may be in a conflict of interest
`a connected person with a clean standing`   MEANS `Person connected with a testing body` OF `a clean standing`, FALSE
`a connected person with a disqualifying conviction` MEANS `Person connected with a testing body` OF `a disqualifying conviction`, FALSE
`a connected person under a pending proceeding` MEANS `Person connected with a testing body` OF `a pending indictment for a disqualifying offence`, FALSE
`a connected person under investigation`     MEANS `Person connected with a testing body` OF `an investigation for a disqualifying offence`, FALSE
`a connected person who may be in a conflict` MEANS `Person connected with a testing body` OF `a clean standing`, TRUE

-- Corporation: incorporated, registered, itself, officers and controllers, proved, further conditions, already a testing body
--                                                                                       inc    reg    itself                                         officers and controllers                                                                                         proved  further          already
`a qualifying corporation`                  MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  `a connected person with a clean standing`,             (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`, `a connected person with a clean standing`),     TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation not incorporated in Israel`  MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF FALSE, TRUE,  `a connected person with a clean standing`,             (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation not registered in Israel`    MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE,  FALSE, `a connected person with a clean standing`,             (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation with a convicted officer`    MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  `a connected person with a clean standing`,             (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`, `a connected person with a disqualifying conviction`), TRUE, NOTHING,    FALSE
`a corporation with a controller facing proceedings` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, `a connected person with a clean standing`,     (LIST `a connected person under a pending proceeding`, `a connected person with a clean standing`),  TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation that was itself convicted`   MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  `a connected person with a disqualifying conviction`, (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation whose employment of testers is not proved` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, `a connected person with a clean standing`, (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 FALSE,  NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation with an officer who may be in a conflict` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, `a connected person with a clean standing`, (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`, `a connected person who may be in a conflict`), TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation that may itself be in a conflict` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, `a connected person who may be in a conflict`,   (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation failing its tender conditions` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE,  `a connected person with a clean standing`,             (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 TRUE,   (JUST FALSE),    FALSE
`a corporation meeting its tender conditions` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE,  `a connected person with a clean standing`,             (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 TRUE,   (JUST TRUE),     FALSE
`a corporation with an officer under investigation` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, `a connected person with a clean standing`,       (LIST `a connected person under investigation`),                                                   TRUE,   NOTHING,         FALSE
`a corporation that is already a testing body` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, `a connected person with a clean standing`,          (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                 TRUE,   NOTHING,         TRUE
`a corporation already a testing body that proved nothing` MEANS `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, `a connected person with a clean standing`, (LIST `a connected person with a clean standing`),                                                FALSE,  NOTHING,         TRUE

§§ `s 35 -- Conditions to serve as a testing body`

-- s.35(1) (src:291): incorporated AND registered in Israel.
#ASSERT `s 35(1) — the corporation is incorporated and registered in Israel` `a qualifying corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(1) — the corporation is incorporated and registered in Israel` `a corporation not incorporated in Israel`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(1) — the corporation is incorporated and registered in Israel` `a corporation not registered in Israel`

-- s.35(2) (src:292): the corporation, an officer or a controller: no disqualifying conviction, no pending proceeding for one.
#ASSERT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a disqualifying conviction`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a clean standing`
-- A conviction counts only if it is for an offence that makes the person unfit.
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a conviction that does not disqualify`
#ASSERT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a pending indictment for a disqualifying offence`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a pending indictment for a minor offence`
-- The judgements with nothing on record disqualify nobody.
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `judgements with nothing on record`
-- Fork F-OFFENCE: a conviction counts only if criminal on the reading taken; a disciplinary conviction counts on the alternative.
`a disciplinary conviction on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a disqualifying disciplinary conviction` MEANS `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF `a disciplinary conviction on record`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a disqualifying disciplinary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 35(2), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a disqualifying disciplinary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 35(2), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a disqualifying conviction`
#ASSERT `s 35(2), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a pending indictment for a disqualifying offence`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a clean standing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a conviction that does not disqualify`
-- Fork F-PROCEEDING: an investigation is no pending criminal proceeding on the reading taken, and is one on the broader.
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `an investigation for a disqualifying offence`
#ASSERT `s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding or investigation is pending on suspicion of one` `an investigation for a disqualifying offence`
#ASSERT `s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding or investigation is pending on suspicion of one` `a disqualifying conviction`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding or investigation is pending on suspicion of one` `a clean standing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding or investigation is pending on suspicion of one` `judgements with nothing on record`
-- Across the corporation, its officers and its controllers.
#ASSERT `s 35(2) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding` `a qualifying corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding` `a corporation with a convicted officer`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding` `a corporation with a controller facing proceedings`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding` `a corporation that was itself convicted`
#ASSERT `s 35(2) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding` `a corporation with an officer under investigation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding or investigation` `a corporation with an officer under investigation`
#ASSERT `s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding or investigation` `a qualifying corporation`

-- s.35(3) (src:293): proved to the Minister's satisfaction.
#ASSERT `s 35(3) — the corporation proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required` `a qualifying corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(3) — the corporation proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required` `a corporation whose employment of testers is not proved`
-- Fork F-LOOP: read strictly (a tester being an employee of a testing body), no corporation that is not yet a
-- testing body can meet (3), so none can ever become one.
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(3), strictly — the corporation proved that it employs testers, a tester being an employee of a testing body` `a qualifying corporation`
#ASSERT `s 35(3), strictly — the corporation proved that it employs testers, a tester being an employee of a testing body` `a corporation that is already a testing body`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(3), strictly — the corporation proved that it employs testers, a tester being an employee of a testing body` `a corporation already a testing body that proved nothing`

-- s.35(4) (src:294): neither the corporation nor an officer or controller may be in a conflict of interest.
#ASSERT `s 35(4) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller may be in a conflict of interest` `a qualifying corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(4) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller may be in a conflict of interest` `a corporation with an officer who may be in a conflict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(4) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller may be in a conflict of interest` `a corporation that may itself be in a conflict`

-- s.35(5) (src:295): further conditions "if set": none set means none to meet.
#ASSERT `s 35(5) — the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement, if any, are met` `a qualifying corporation`
#ASSERT `s 35(5) — the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement, if any, are met` `a corporation meeting its tender conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(5) — the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement, if any, are met` `a corporation failing its tender conditions`

-- s.35 as a whole (src:289-290): all five.
#ASSERT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a qualifying corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation not incorporated in Israel`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation not registered in Israel`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation with a convicted officer`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation with a controller facing proceedings`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation that was itself convicted`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation whose employment of testers is not proved`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation with an officer who may be in a conflict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation that may itself be in a conflict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation failing its tender conditions`
#ASSERT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation meeting its tender conditions`
#ASSERT `s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` `a corporation with an officer under investigation`

§§ `s 36 -- Authorisation of testers and experts`

-- Person: standing, may be in a conflict, meets the regulations' conditions (if the caller says), the Minister found
-- unfitting circumstances, gave reasons, a written hearing was given, the Minister refused
--                                                                         standing                      conflict  regulations      found  reasons  hearing  refused
`an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions` MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, (JUST TRUE),  FALSE, FALSE,   FALSE,   FALSE
`an applicant failing the regulations' conditions` MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, (JUST FALSE), FALSE, FALSE,   FALSE,   FALSE
`an applicant for whom the regulations are not stated` MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,    FALSE, NOTHING,      FALSE, FALSE,   FALSE,   FALSE
`a barred convict`                                  MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a disqualifying conviction`, FALSE, (JUST TRUE),  FALSE, FALSE,   FALSE,   FALSE
`a barred convict, regulations not stated`          MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a disqualifying conviction`, FALSE, NOTHING,      FALSE, FALSE,   FALSE,   FALSE
`an applicant under a pending proceeding`           MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a pending indictment for a disqualifying offence`, FALSE, (JUST TRUE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an applicant under a pending proceeding for a minor offence` MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a pending indictment for a minor offence`, FALSE, (JUST TRUE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an applicant who may be in a conflict`             MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        TRUE,  (JUST TRUE),  FALSE, FALSE,   FALSE,   FALSE
`an applicant duly refused`                         MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, (JUST TRUE),  TRUE,  TRUE,    TRUE,    TRUE
`an applicant refused with no reasons`              MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, (JUST TRUE),  TRUE,  FALSE,   TRUE,    TRUE
`an applicant refused with no hearing`              MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, (JUST TRUE),  TRUE,  TRUE,    FALSE,   TRUE
`an applicant refused with no finding of unfitness` MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, (JUST TRUE),  FALSE, TRUE,    TRUE,    TRUE
`an applicant who could be refused but was not`     MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, (JUST TRUE),  TRUE,  TRUE,    TRUE,    FALSE
`an applicant duly refused, regulations not stated` MEANS `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` OF `a clean standing`,        FALSE, NOTHING,      TRUE,  TRUE,    TRUE,    TRUE

-- s.36(a) (src:298): the regulations' conditions are the caller's to state; unstated is a named refusal, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 36(a) — the person meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c)` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(a) — the person meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c)` `an applicant failing the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(a) — the person meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c)` `an applicant for whom the regulations are not stated`
        BECAUSE "no regulations under section 60(1)(c) are in the sources, and the caller has not said whether the person meets their conditions"

-- s.36(b) (src:300-301): the bar.
#ASSERT `s 36(b)(1) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a barred convict`
#ASSERT `s 36(b)(1) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `an applicant under a pending proceeding`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(b)(1) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `an applicant under a pending proceeding for a minor offence`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(b)(1) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT `s 36(b)(2) — the person may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` `an applicant who may be in a conflict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(b)(2) — the person may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` `a barred convict`
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` `an applicant under a pending proceeding`
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` `an applicant who may be in a conflict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` `an applicant under a pending proceeding for a minor offence`

-- s.36(a) and (b) together: may the Minister authorise?  A barred person is answered FALSE before the regulations
-- are asked, so even with the regulations unstated the answer is FALSE, not a refusal.
#ASSERT `s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` `an applicant failing the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` `a barred convict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` `a barred convict, regulations not stated`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` `an applicant who may be in a conflict`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` `an applicant for whom the regulations are not stated`

-- s.36(c) (src:302): refusal needs the finding, the reasons and the written hearing.
#ASSERT `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` `an applicant duly refused`
#ASSERT `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` `an applicant who could be refused but was not`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` `an applicant refused with no reasons`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` `an applicant refused with no hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` `an applicant refused with no finding of unfitness`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT `s 36(c) — the Minister validly refused to authorise the person` `an applicant duly refused`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister validly refused to authorise the person` `an applicant who could be refused but was not`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister validly refused to authorise the person` `an applicant refused with no reasons`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister validly refused to authorise the person` `an applicant refused with no hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister validly refused to authorise the person` `an applicant refused with no finding of unfitness`

-- The duty of s.36(a): the Minister must authorise unless barred or validly refused.  A refusal without reasons,
-- hearing or finding does not discharge it.
#ASSERT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant who could be refused but was not`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant failing the regulations' conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `a barred convict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `a barred convict, regulations not stated`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant who may be in a conflict`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant duly refused`
#ASSERT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant refused with no reasons`
#ASSERT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant refused with no hearing`
#ASSERT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant refused with no finding of unfitness`
-- A duly refused person is answered before the regulations are asked.
#ASSERT NOT `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant duly refused, regulations not stated`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant for whom the regulations are not stated`

-- Fork F-DUTY: read as a power, the same person may be authorised and the Minister need not.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 7
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `a barred convict` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 7

-- The three rules on the person, traced.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(a) — the Minister shall authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 7
-- No time is stated, so waiting breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(a) — the Minister shall authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- No duty arises for a barred person, a person who failed the conditions, or one duly refused.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(a) — the Minister shall authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `a barred convict` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(a) — the Minister shall authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant failing the regulations' conditions` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(a) — the Minister shall authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant duly refused` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- A refusal that lacked reasons does not end the duty.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(a) — the Minister shall authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant refused with no reasons` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- s.36(b): authorising a barred person is a breach; authorising one who is not barred offends nothing.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 36(b) — the Minister shall not authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `a barred convict` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 3
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 36(b) — the Minister shall not authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant who may be in a conflict` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 3
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(b) — the Minister shall not authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant meeting the regulations' conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 3
-- s.36(c): a proper refusal is the Minister using his power; one without reasons is not accepted.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant duly refused` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `refuse to authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant refused with no reasons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `refuse to authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person as a tester or an expert` `an applicant refused with no hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `refuse to authorise a person as a tester or an expert` AT 3

§§ `s 36(d) -- conditions and instructions in the instrument`

-- src:303.  Setting needs no hearing.  Changing follows a written hearing and, on reading A, concerns only
-- conditions or instructions as to modes of action; reading B covers work procedures too (fork F-CHANGE).
-- Change: kind, a written hearing was given
`a change as to modes of action after a hearing`    MEANS `Change under section 36(d)` OF `a condition or instruction as to modes of action`,  TRUE
`a change as to modes of action with no hearing`    MEANS `Change under section 36(d)` OF `a condition or instruction as to modes of action`,  FALSE
`a change as to work procedures after a hearing`    MEANS `Change under section 36(d)` OF `a condition or instruction as to work procedures`, TRUE
`a change as to work procedures with no hearing`    MEANS `Change under section 36(d)` OF `a condition or instruction as to work procedures`, FALSE
#ASSERT `s 36(d) — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to modes of action after a hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(d) — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to modes of action with no hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(d) — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to work procedures after a hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(d) — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to work procedures with no hearing`
#ASSERT `s 36(d), reading B — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action or work procedures, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to modes of action after a hearing`
#ASSERT `s 36(d), reading B — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action or work procedures, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to work procedures after a hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(d), reading B — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action or work procedures, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to modes of action with no hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(d), reading B — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action or work procedures, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to work procedures with no hearing`

`the change as to modes of action after a hearing, made` MEANS `change a condition or instruction in the instrument of authorisation` `a change as to modes of action after a hearing`
`the change as to work procedures after a hearing, made` MEANS `change a condition or instruction in the instrument of authorisation` `a change as to work procedures after a hearing`
`the change as to modes of action with no hearing, made` MEANS `change a condition or instruction in the instrument of authorisation` `a change as to modes of action with no hearing`

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(d) — the Minister may set conditions and instructions in the instrument of authorisation` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `set conditions and instructions in the instrument of authorisation as to modes of action and work procedures` AT 1
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(d) — the Minister may change a condition or instruction he gave as to modes of action, after a written hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the change as to modes of action after a hearing, made` AT 4
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(d) — the Minister may change a condition or instruction he gave as to modes of action, after a written hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the change as to work procedures after a hearing, made` AT 4
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(d) — the Minister may change a condition or instruction he gave as to modes of action, after a written hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the change as to modes of action with no hearing, made` AT 4
-- Reading B accepts the work-procedures change.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 36(d), reading B — the Minister may change a condition or instruction he gave, after a written hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the change as to work procedures after a hearing, made` AT 4
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 36(d), reading B — the Minister may change a condition or instruction he gave, after a written hearing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the change as to modes of action with no hearing, made` AT 4

§§ `s 36(e) -- the period of the authorisation (P23)`

-- src:304.  Granted on Thursday 2026-01-01.  30 days from it end on 2026-01-31 (s.10(a)).  The grant day is a day
-- of the authorisation; the last day is inside; the day after is outside.
`an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026` MEANS `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (JUST (`a number of days fixed in the instrument` 30))
`an instrument of 1 month from 31 January 2025` MEANS `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` OF (YMD 2025 1 31), (JUST (`a number of months fixed in the instrument` 1))
`an instrument of 1 year from 29 February 2024` MEANS `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` OF (YMD 2024 2 29), (JUST (`a number of years fixed in the instrument` 1))
`an instrument to 15 March 2026` MEANS `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (JUST (`a last day fixed in the instrument` (YMD 2026 3 15)))
`an instrument that fixes no period` MEANS `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 1 month from 31 January 2025` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 1 year from 29 February 2024` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument to 15 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 31) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2025 2 28) `under` `an instrument of 1 month from 31 January 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2025 3 1) `under` `an instrument of 1 month from 31 January 2025`
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 3 15) `under` `an instrument to 15 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 3 16) `under` `an instrument to 15 March 2026`
-- The instrument fixes no period and s.36(e) supplies none: a named refusal, never a number.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument that fixes no period`
        BECAUSE "the instrument of authorisation fixes no period, and s 36(e) gives no default"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 15) `under` `an instrument that fixes no period`

-- Fork F-P23 (kind V, s.10(c) not applied): a nominal last day that is a rest day stays the last day; the
-- alternative moves it to the next day that is not a rest day.
`a calendar with 31 January 2026 a rest day` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 1 31)
`a calendar with 31 January and 1 February 2026 rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 1 31, YMD 2026 2 1)
`a calendar with 28 February and 1 March 2025 rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2025 2 28, YMD 2025 3 1)
`a calendar with no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026` `a calendar with 31 January 2026 a rest day` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026` `a calendar with 31 January and 1 February 2026 rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 2
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 1 month from 31 January 2025` `a calendar with 28 February and 1 March 2025 rest days` EQUALS YMD 2025 3 2
-- A last day the instrument names is a date, not a counted period: s.10(c) does not move it.
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument to 15 March 2026` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument that fixes no period` `a calendar with no rest days`

-- Fork F-START: on the alternative the authorisation begins the day AFTER it was granted.
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), beginning the day after the grant — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), beginning the day after the grant — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 2) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `s 36(e), beginning the day after the grant — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 31) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e), beginning the day after the grant — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
